00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:25.380
Just like anytime you're
working with any database,

00:04:25.380 --> 00:04:27.990
you generally provide
a set of credentials,

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:31.950
and it's these credentials
that basically shape the view

00:04:31.950 --> 00:04:34.200
of the data that
the AI will see,

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:38.700
so you can use a proxy
user that's tied

00:04:38.700 --> 00:04:41.540
to your identity domain,
and that can be used

00:04:41.540 --> 00:04:44.480
to determine what type of data
you can see in the tables

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:47.630
or whether the tables
are even visible at all.

00:04:47.630 --> 00:04:50.790
Once you have the connection
defined, you can go ahead

00:04:50.790 --> 00:04:53.010
and create the MCP server,
