an MCP server group.

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:09.150
That will give him privileges
to connect to and talk

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:15.840
to our MCP server using his
existing Azure Entra ID login.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:19.380
At that point, I'm going
to define the MCP tools.

00:05:19.380 --> 00:05:25.480
Tools are sort of the APIs
that allow clients for the MCP

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:30.600
or the agents that are speaking
MCP protocol to our server.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.430
This is where they can
request things to be done

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:36.060
on their behalf, and probably
the most well-known pattern is

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:38.160
natural language to SQL.

00:05:38.160 --> 00:05:39.720
Ram, in his demo, I
think is probably going

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.920
to say something like,
"Hey, Mr. AI Wizard,

00:05:43.920 --> 00:05:47.790
