into a query statement

00:05:51.540 --> 00:05:53.790
that our database will
understand, and it'll submit

00:05:53.790 --> 00:05:56.820
that query to be ran
through our MCP tool.

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:58.080
Before you can do that though,

00:05:58.080 --> 00:06:02.400
we're going to register the
agent as an MCP client,

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:05.340
and that's what allows the
OAuth 2 workflow to work.

00:06:05.340 --> 00:06:07.260
The first time you'll
go to do this,

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:09.360
which we probably won't show
in the demo because it's kind

00:06:09.360 --> 00:06:12.690
